  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models (0.48–0.52) vastly outperform image-only models (0.21–0.23), and among RNA encoders, scvi_n200 (0.5203) beats pca_n2000 (0.4849) by ~3.5 pts, indicating learned representations matter. However, we have zero evidence on whether the multiprofile setting with aggregation improves over singleprofile. Question: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) directly compares against config_004 (same encoder, singleprofile) to isolate the effect of multiprofile + simple aggregation. Why this is the best next experiment: it uses the strongest known encoder, tests the simplest aggregation (avgpool) to establish a lower bound on multiprofile benefit, and provides a clean single-variable comparison. If avgpool helps, transformer aggregation becomes a justified follow-up; if it does not, we avoid spending budget on more complex aggregation schemes. This resolves a fundamental architectural question (single vs. multi-profile) before committing to multimodal fusion experiments, which would change multiple variables simultaneously."
}

